## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of enterprise-scale data pipeline challenges including multi-region architecture, schema evolution management, data governance compliance, automated recovery mechanisms, and observability patterns in production environments.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-region data residency enforcement with tenant isolation
- Schema evolution and drift detection at ingestion boundaries
- Quarantine workflows for non-conforming data preservation
- SLA-driven automated backfill with replay mechanisms
- Distributed tracing with OpenTelemetry across regional boundaries
- Idempotent processing patterns and cost-optimized resource allocation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Schema validation with tenant awareness
function validateRecord(record, tenantSchema) {
  if (record.schemaVersion !== tenantSchema.version) {
    return { valid: false, reason: 'schema_version_mismatch' };
  }

  const requiredFields = tenantSchema.fields.filter(f => f.required);
  const missingFields = requiredFields.filter(f => !(f.name in record));

  return missingFields.length === 0 
    ? { valid: true } 
    : { valid: false, reason: 'missing_fields', fields: missingFields };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This interview question explores cross-region, multi-tenant data routing with dynamic policy-driven enrichment, end-to-end observability, and integration of AWS data primitives beyond basic pipelines.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-region routing with tenant isolation
- OPA-driven enrichment at ingestion with hot policy refresh via changelog stream
- Idempotent writes to S3 Parquet and DynamoDB
- AWS Glue catalog integration with Athena for analytics
- OpenTelemetry end-to-end tracing
- Per-tenant DLQ handling and retry strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: ingestion Lambda
async function processRecord(record, ctx) {
  const tenantId = extractTenantId(record);
  const region = extractRegion(record);
  const enriched = await enrichWithOPARules(record, tenantId);
  await writeToS3Parquet(enriched, tenantId, region);
  await writeToDynamoDB(enriched, tenantId);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests schema-versioned validation, deduplication, and lineage in a minimal, real-world pipeline. It ensures handling of schema evolution while keeping the flow beginner-friendly.

## Key Concepts
- Kinesis ingestion and Lambda processing
- Schema-versioned validation and conditional logic
- DynamoDB dedupe by composite key (deviceId+ts)
- Parquet writes to S3 partitioned by region/date/schema_version
- DLQ, CloudWatch lineage logging, backfill planning

## Code Example
```javascript
function validate(record){
  if (record.schema_version===1){
    return Boolean(record.deviceId && record.ts && record.temp);
  } else {
    return Boolean(record.deviceId && record.ts && record.temp && record.battery && record.location);
  }
}
```

